---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title="About" description="About Érico Perez Neto" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <section class="section-hero">
        <div class="wrap">
          <div class="stack-32">
            <h1 class="h-display">About</h1>

            <div class="stack-16">
              <span class="label">Background</span>
              <div class="content-width stack-16">
                <p class="v-p300 text-text-t900">
                  I’m Érico, a Staff Engineer based in São Paulo. I’ve been writing software for 30
                  years, with the last 16 dedicated to Apple platforms — primarily iOS apps in
                  environments where stability isn’t optional (banking, payments, fintech), reaching
                  tens of millions of users. More recently I’ve also been contributing to open
                  source, writing command-line tools for Swift codebases — available for macOS and
                  Linux.
                </p>
                <p class="v-p300 text-text-t900">
                  That work made me serious about the small stuff — test discipline, code
                  organization, the habit of catching weak assertions before they ship. The <a
                    href="/open-source/"
                    class="link-inline">open source CLIs</a
                  > you’ll find here grew out of problems I kept running into: measuring test effectiveness
                  honestly, surfacing structural duplication, and enforcing a predictable shape for Swift
                  types.
                </p>
                <p class="v-p300 text-text-t900">
                  Most of my work has been at Staff and Principal levels at companies like Itaú
                  Rede, Creditas, ThoughtWorks, and PagSeguro. At Rede in particular, alongside
                  mobile architecture, I designed the backend contracts and integrations that mobile
                  clients depend on — work that made me think about the API and the device as one
                  system, not two.
                </p>
                <p class="v-p300 text-text-t900">
                  This site is where I share what I build and write about what I learn along the
                  way.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="stack-16">
              <span class="label">Skills</span>
              <div class="chip-list">
                <span class="chip">Swift</span>
                <span class="chip">SwiftUI</span>
                <span class="chip">UIKit</span>
                <span class="chip">Objective-C</span>
                <span class="chip">Go</span>
                <span class="chip">Swift Concurrency</span>
                <span class="chip">iOS</span>
                <span class="chip">macOS</span>
                <span class="chip">Multi-platform CLIs</span>
                <span class="chip">Clean Architecture</span>
                <span class="chip">Modularization</span>
                <span class="chip">MVVM</span>
                <span class="chip">Design System</span>
                <span class="chip">Server-Driven UI</span>
                <span class="chip">XCTest</span>
                <span class="chip">Swift Testing</span>
                <span class="chip">Mutation Testing</span>
                <span class="chip">Snapshot Testing</span>
                <span class="chip">TDD</span>
                <span class="chip">REST</span>
                <span class="chip">GraphQL</span>
                <span class="chip">Distributed Systems</span>
                <span class="chip">Event-driven Architecture</span>
                <span class="chip">Xcode</span>
                <span class="chip">SPM</span>
                <span class="chip">GitHub Actions</span>
                <span class="chip">Fastlane</span>
                <span class="chip">Datadog</span>
                <span class="chip">Firebase</span>
                <span class="chip">Claude</span>
                <span class="chip">Claude Code</span>
                <span class="chip">MCP</span>
                <span class="chip">Prompt Engineering</span>
                <span class="chip">RAG</span>
                <span class="chip">AI Agents</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <a href="/contact/" class="link-arrow self-start"
              >Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
